# Fixed 2026-10-02, defect 135's class, lane literals: the other half of
# `fixedbugs-135-l5-an-uppercase-prefix-with-no-digits`. Where the digits
# after an uppercase prefix faulted, `0XG`, `0B2` or `0X_FF`, the run told
# that mistake in the first run, so lowering the prefix adds none and stays
# certain: `check --apply` writes `0xG`, `0b2` and `0x_FF`, and what is left
# is the mistake the first run already named (`number.hero`).

function a_letter_past_the_base()
    print(0XG)  #~ digit_not_in_base base_prefix_case

function a_digit_past_the_base()
    print(0B2)  #~ digit_not_in_base base_prefix_case

function a_separator_first()
    print(0X_FF)  #~ misplaced_separator base_prefix_case
